---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import PolicyContact from "../components/PolicyContact.astro";
import { LEGAL_HOLDER } from "../data/site";

const REPO = "https://github.com/curthenrichs/the-bead-reserve";
---

<Layout
  title="The Bead Reserve : Terms"
  description="The terms for using The Bead Reserve's website, covering the status of the token and the license for the code."
>
  <main>
    <article class="policy bracket-frame">
      <h1>Terms</h1>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>Last updated: October 7, 2026</p>
        <p>
          These terms cover the website of The Bead Reserve, operated by
          {LEGAL_HOLDER}. Use of the site constitutes acceptance of these terms.
        </p>

        <h2>The token</h2>
        <p>
          BEADZ is a novelty collectible issued for amusement. It has no
          monetary value, and none is promised. It carries no expectation of
          profit. It is not a stablecoin, a security, a deposit, or a payment
          instrument, and is not pegged to any national currency. The Reserve
          sells it to no one and seeds no market. Any market a third party
          creates is that party's doing and risk.
        </p>
        <p>
          Physical redemption is available by prepaid certified mail with
          signature, in minimum lots, while the redemption window is open. It
          costs far more than the beads are worth. The
          <a href="/whitepaper.pdf">whitepaper</a> sets out the full terms.
        </p>
        <p>Nothing on this site is financial or legal advice.</p>

        <h2>Code</h2>
        <p>
          The software behind The Bead Reserve, this site included, is published
          under the <a href={`${REPO}/blob/main/LICENSE`}>MIT license</a> in the
          <a href={REPO}>public repository</a>. Anything the license allows is
          allowed here, provided the copyright and license notice travel with
          the code.
        </p>

        <h2>Brand assets</h2>
        <p>
          Henry and the reserve seal are excluded from that grant under the
          BRAND ASSETS EXCEPTION in the repository's <code>LICENSE</code>. They
          are &copy; {LEGAL_HOLDER}, all rights reserved. They may be used to
          refer to The Bead Reserve. Neither they nor the name "The Bead
          Reserve" may be used as the identity of another project, a fork of
          this one included. The <a href="/brand/">brand assets</a> page sets
          out the usage rules.
        </p>

        <h2>No warranty</h2>
        <p>
          The site and the token are provided "as is" and "as available",
          without warranties of any kind, express or implied. The reserve is
          uninsured. To the maximum extent permitted by law, {LEGAL_HOLDER} is
          not liable for any damages arising from use of the site or the token,
          or from reliance on the site's content.
        </p>

        <h2>Indemnity</h2>
        <p>
          Anyone who forks the software or deploys their own vault does so at
          their own risk. They agree to indemnify and hold harmless
          {LEGAL_HOLDER} against claims arising from that use, to the extent the
          law allows.
        </p>

        <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
        <p>
          The site links to the Half-Built Robots blog and to other sites. Those
          sites are outside this site's control, and a link is not an
          endorsement. Their terms and privacy practices are their own.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes</h2>
        <p>
          These terms may change. Revisions are posted on this page with a new
          date at the top. Continued use of the site after a change constitutes
          acceptance of the revised terms.
        </p>

        <h2>Governing law</h2>
        <p>
          These terms are governed by the laws of the State of California,
          United States.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <PolicyContact />
      </div>
    </article>
  </main>
</Layout>
